@startuml
title M-SH3 - Approval and delivery evidence (SH2+ target; schema pending)
hide empty description

state "Delivery receipt vocabulary\ndurable state owner: swarma-session-host service" as Receipts {
  state "accepted" as Accepted
  state "queued" as Queued
  state "dispatched" as Dispatched
  state "applied" as Applied
  state "refused" as Refused
  state "expired" as Expired
  state "unknown" as Unknown
  state "Redelivery permitted" as Redelivery
  Dispatched --> Unknown : host / runner failure between dispatch and application
  Unknown --> Applied : matching input marker in intact transcript
  Unknown --> Redelivery : confirmed marker absence in intact transcript
  Unknown --> Unknown : unresolved evidence; keep fence closed
  note right of Queued
    Closed fence may queue, never deliver.
    No acknowledgement without durable host write.
    Full accepted/queued/dispatched/refused/expired transition schema:
    unspecified in spec §3.4 / §7; vocabulary is not an invented pipeline.
  end note
  note right of Redelivery
    Reconcile before fence reopening; ordinary input may redeliver
    with sender/message-id dedup and idempotent op_id (§3.4, §3.7).
    Unknown approval answer / control effect MUST NOT auto-replay.
  end note
}

state "Pending native interaction / approval\nstate and authority owner: host service" as Approval {
  state "Pending native interaction" as Pending
  state "First valid resolution accepted" as Resolved
  state "Expired interaction" as ApprovalExpired
  state "Invalidated by fence / restart" as Invalidated
  Pending --> Resolved : authorised current execution/epoch; exact digest; unexpired; first CAS
  Pending --> ApprovalExpired : interaction expiry; later answer cannot resolve it
  Pending --> Invalidated : fence closes; historical approval invalid on restart
  Pending --> Pending : refuse wrong authority / execution / epoch / digest; ordinary user turn is not resolution
  Resolved --> Resolved : refuse later resolution; first-valid CAS already accepted
  ApprovalExpired --> ApprovalExpired : refuse expired answer
  Invalidated --> Invalidated : refuse stale answer
  note right of Pending
    Bind execution, turn, native request digest, options and expiry.
    Automatic approval requires explicit allowlist policy.
    Refused attempt does not imply a valid pending interaction was resolved.
    These are conceptual views, not new wire field names or enum values.
    Approval wire/state schema and allowlist values: unspecified in spec §7.
  end note
}

note bottom of Approval
  Process identities: swarma-session-host under its service account admits
  and records; swarma-session-runner under worker-<label> owns the transport;
  Claude Code / private Codex app-server produces native interactions.
  Authorised caller resolves them; precise approval principal roles and
  request/ack protocol are unspecified in spec §3.4 / §7.
  Host transcript/audit evidence is service-private, not agent-writable.
  Runner-side persistent delivery marker layout: unspecified in spec §3.4.
  Current / SH1 keeps existing adapter behavior; these semantics require
  dedicated schema publication and testing before SH2+ activation.
end note

legend bottom
